  "details": "I know performance issues are super difficult to diagnose, however I am definitely experiencing a performance regression in VRChat since the past few versions. In situations where I previously would just have a low framerate, turning my head results in seconds-long freezes. The frequency and duration of the freezes seems to increase with the number of visible avatars, as well as how quickly I turn my head. In some cases, turning my head towards a group of players can freeze my game solid for ~10 seconds, and once it recovers the framerate is stuck very low, **until I rejoin the instance** . Re-joining the instance and approaching the same group of players, the framerate remains high with no issues, until the next random head-turning-induced stutter.\n\nPC Specs: Ryzen 5600X, 48GB DDR4 RAM, RTX 3080 10GB VRAM",
